### 3. Tangent Function: $f(x) = \tan(x)$

#### Visual
```tikz
\begin{tikzpicture}[scale=1.5, transform shape]
    % Axes
    \draw[->, thick] (-6.5, 0) -- (6.5, 0) node[right] {$x$};
    \draw[->, thick] (0, -3.5) -- (0, 3.5) node[above] {$y$};
    \foreach \x in {-6, -4, -2, 2, 4, 6}
        \draw (\x, 0.1) -- (\x, -0.1) node[below] {$\x$};
    \foreach \y in {-3, -2, -1, 1, 2, 3}
        \draw (0.1, \y) -- (-0.1, \y) node[left] {$\y$};

    % Grid
    \draw[gray!30, dashed] (-6.5, -3.5) grid (6.5, 3.5);

    % Tangent function
    \draw[green, very thick, domain=-1.57:1.57, samples=100] plot (\x, {tan(\x r)});
    \draw[green, very thick, domain=1.57:4.71, samples=100] plot (\x, {tan(\x r)});
    \draw[green, very thick, domain=4.71:6.28, samples=100] plot (\x, {tan(\x r)});
    \draw[green, very thick, domain=-6.28:-4.71, samples=100] plot (\x, {tan(\x r)});
    \draw[green, very thick, domain=-4.71:-1.57, samples=100] plot (\x, {tan(\x r)});

    % Asymptotes
    \draw[red, dashed, thick] (1.57, -3.5) -- (1.57, 3.5);
    \draw[red, dashed, thick] (-1.57, -3.5) -- (-1.57, 3.5);
    \draw[red, dashed, thick] (4.71, -3.5) -- (4.71, 3.5);
    \draw[red, dashed, thick] (-4.71, -3.5) -- (-4.71, 3.5);

    % Key points
    \filldraw[black] (0,0) circle (2pt) node[below right] {$(0,0)$};
    \filldraw[black] (1.57,0) circle (2pt) node[below] {$\frac{\pi}{2}$};
    \filldraw[black] (-1.57,0) circle (2pt) node[below] {$-\frac{\pi}{2}$};
    \filldraw[black] (3.14,0) circle (2pt) node[below] {$\pi$};
    \filldraw[black] (-3.14,0) circle (2pt) node[below] {$-\pi$};
\end{tikzpicture}
```

#### Key Characteristics:
- **Period**: $\pi$
- **Range**: $(-\infty, \infty)$
- **Vertical Asymptotes**: At $x = \frac{\pi}{2} + k\pi$ for any integer $k$
- **Key Points**:
  - $(0, 0)$
  - $(\frac{\pi}{4}, 1)$
  - $(-\frac{\pi}{4}, -1)$
  - $(\frac{3\pi}{4}, -1)$
  - $(-\frac{3\pi}{4}, 1)$

